---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';
import { fillDurations } from '../lib/time';

// DRAFT copy: every claim here comes from the spec. Cut any value sentence
// that isn't true, per the spec's Values section.
const meta = fillDurations('{meta}');
---

<Base title="About" description={`About ${profile.name}, ${profile.role}.`}>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    I'm a {profile.role.toLowerCase()}. I spent {meta} at Meta, seven of them owning performance and reliability for
    Instagram on Android.
  </p>

  <p>
    The work I'm best at starts with a symptom nobody can explain: a crash rate that won't move, a screen that judders,
    an incident that keeps coming back. I find the cause, fix it, and then build whatever stops it returning, whether
    that's a lint rule, a dashboard, a training programme or an agent that does the first hour of debugging.
  </p>

  <h2>What I care about</h2>

  <p>
    <strong>Craft.</strong> I write down the options I rejected as well as the one I chose, and this site holds itself to
    a published performance and accessibility budget.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Leverage through people.</strong> The Reliability Captain programme I founded trained 12 engineers to run
    incidents, and it kept running after I moved on.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Open work.</strong> This site has no tracking scripts, and its source is public.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Safe, useful AI.</strong> I build agents that debug production systems, and I write about where they fail as
    well as where they help.
  </p>

  <h2>What's next</h2>
  <p>
    I'm looking for work where a large system needs to get faster, steadier or easier to operate. That covers SRE,
    performance, platform, Android and AI infrastructure.
  </p>

  <p><a href="/resume/">Read my resume</a> or <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a>.</p>
</Base>
